 following is the graph of $y =-5^{x} - 3$?" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={5}^{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938518/assets/e85f2f0f042f85b5f7c8162b744a5c9d4688a93faf4ccddbad82ca1a9db47f93.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{5}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938518/assets/971d4cf0310cced68f72be500d65fff26163a7e2bd5cee005e25e92ca3fb931e.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $3$ units down to give $y=-{5}^{x}-3.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,-4)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938518/assets/8d4dd11693eda60dc0ed7eb041bdb94c90757f6bb75be3523ce77d01d28534de.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0f61a7c3-82e6-5f90-8a95-4a79078fd542" :knowledge-point/title "Vertical Reflections of Exponential Growth Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c6dfba-701c-5306-b3a7-3ea2e70bd12d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938518/assets/d4811fb906db8a9326ae35826aa5ab2b3795d890c7a5f21862419206cecbcf83.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247719} {:answer/id #uuid "1832956c-e7c0-5e16-93b3-734278e95fb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938518/assets/1c31f62568e601154d960de5d0a046ad9e1aeb4fa5eafefcd82abb4205797c77.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247720} {:answer/id #uuid "79dce51d-8561-5e84-b348-13d1732334f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_